#exception-box(title: "THE SEVEN FATAL CUET TRAPS")[
  1. *BAMCEF vs BSP:* BAMCEF (1978) was a *non-political employee federation*; the BSP (1984) was the formal *electoral political party*.
  2. *Dalit Panthers Location:* Founded in *Maharashtra* (Bombay slums) in 1972, NOT in Uttar Pradesh or Bihar.
  3. *Opening of Locks Date:* The Faizabad Court ordered the locks opened in *February 1986*, NOT in 1992 (the year of demolition).
  4. *CM Resignation on 6 Dec 1992:* *Kalyan Singh* was the ruling BJP Chief Minister who resigned, NOT Mulayam Singh Yadav (who was in opposition).
  5. *Inquiry Commission for Ayodhya:* The *Liberhan Commission* investigated the Babri demolition; the *Nanavati Commission* probed 1984 & 2002 Godhra.
  6. *Best Bakery Case Venue:* The Supreme Court transferred the trial from Gujarat to *Maharashtra* to guarantee a free and fair judicial trial.
  7. *Nature of Indian Secularism:* It is NOT passive or strictly separated; it practices *principled distance*, permitting state social reform while safeguarding minority rights.
]

