== Part 2: Ayodhya Dispute, Judicial Rulings & Communalism

#mcq(6, [In which year did the Faizabad District Court order the opening of the locks of the disputed Babri structure in Ayodhya to allow Hindu devotees to offer worship?], (
  [1949], [February 1986], [1990], [December 1992],
))

#solution(6, [In February 1986, the Faizabad District Judge ordered the locks of the Babri structure opened for Hindu worship, an event that escalated religious mobilization on both sides.], answer: [B])

#mcq(7, [Who was the Chief Minister of Uttar Pradesh who resigned on the evening of 6 December 1992 following the demolition of the Babri Masjid?], (
  [Mulayam Singh Yadav], [Kalyan Singh], [Mayawati], [Rajnath Singh],
))

#solution(7, [Kalyan Singh headed the BJP state government in Uttar Pradesh; he submitted his resignation to the Governor on the evening of 6 December 1992 after the structure was demolished.], answer: [B])

#mcq(8, [Which judicial inquiry commission was appointed by the Government of India in December 1992 to investigate the sequence of events leading to the demolition of the Babri Masjid?], (
  [Shah Commission], [Sarkaria Commission], [Nanavati Commission], [The Justice M.S. Liberhan Commission],
))

#solution(8, [The Justice M.S. Liberhan Commission of Inquiry was constituted in December 1992 to probe the Babri Masjid demolition; it submitted its report in 2009.], answer: [D])

#mcq(9, [In which landmark judgment did a nine-judge bench of the Supreme Court uphold the dismissal of four BJP state governments in 1992, ruling that 'Secularism is part of the Basic Structure'?], (
